195
00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:01.450
Like, there could be this sort of rock-bottomy moment.

196
00:10:01.690 --> 00:10:01.910
Right.

197
00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:02.950
And it's an event.

198
00:10:03.110 --> 00:10:05.550
It's like a big event and everyone's there to witness it.

199
00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:05.990
Yes.

200
00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:11.610
Fast fact number three, I have a talking head observation for this episode.

201
00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:13.670
Oh, I'm so curious.

202
00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:19.770
So, as you re-watch this episode, take a note of the talking heads.

203
00:10:20.630 --> 00:10:26.290
Almost all of them are filmed from different angles than we normally would.

204
00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:31.510
I believe there's only one where someone's seated in the traditional chair with the kind

205
00:10:31.510 --> 00:10:32.670
of party through the blind.

206
00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:33.650
Right.

207
00:10:33.850 --> 00:10:35.090
We're all over the office.

208
00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:36.370
All over the office.

209
00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:41.350
So, this was not just because there was a party happening behind us.

210
00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:47.250
Justin said this was because they wanted to wait until they were in the editing room

211
00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:51.970
to place the talking heads throughout the episode, and they didn't want anything in the

212
00:10:51.970 --> 00:10:58.590
background to, like, in some way mess up their ability to move these talking heads around.

213
00:10:58.750 --> 00:11:02.230
Well, they had probably learned their lesson from that episode, Weight Loss.

214
00:11:02.230 --> 00:11:09.490
Where they had to digitally, it's a hard word to say, they had to digitally change Ed's tie

215
00:11:09.490 --> 00:11:13.470
and shirt because they kept moving the talking heads and what was happening behind them didn't

216
00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:13.870
match.

217
00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:14.410
Yeah.

218
00:11:14.550 --> 00:11:18.550
So, you'll notice even Michael's talking heads, he is not seated at his desk.

219
00:11:18.730 --> 00:11:24.030
He's standing in front of his desk and they purposely framed out the window behind him

220
00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:30.490
because timing-wise, they didn't know if it would be, like, still daytime or if it would

221
00:11:30.490 --> 00:11:31.090
be evening.

222
00:11:31.430 --> 00:11:35.730
So, they really tried to make all the talking heads as totally neutral as possible.

223
00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:36.490
Smart.

224
00:11:36.890 --> 00:11:37.110
Yeah.

225
00:11:37.270 --> 00:11:38.090
And it was kind of fun.

226
00:11:38.270 --> 00:11:43.130
After Justin told me that, I went back and re-watched the episode and it was totally true.

227
00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:43.830
Yeah.

228
00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:48.530
I read the shooting draft and definitely things are moved all around.

229
00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:50.650
So, it's good they did it.

230
00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:50.970
Yeah.

231
00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:52.450
That's all I got.

232
00:11:52.450 --> 00:11:56.870
Well, before we get into this episode, I went digging in my digital clutter.

