And the tree fell on my head.

585
00:27:15.840 --> 00:27:16.100
What?

586
00:27:16.600 --> 00:27:17.800
I fell to the ground.

587
00:27:17.900 --> 00:27:18.960
The tree fell on top of me.

588
00:27:18.960 --> 00:27:25.260
Then I had to drag it down the stairwell, this Christmas tree, out the building, through

589
00:27:25.260 --> 00:27:28.240
the parking lot, all the way to the street.

590
00:27:28.380 --> 00:27:30.300
We filmed all of that.

591
00:27:30.760 --> 00:27:33.180
It legitimately was a physical workout.

592
00:27:33.460 --> 00:27:35.880
I actually like messed up my hair.

593
00:27:36.080 --> 00:27:40.280
I had like scratches on like my hands from the tree trying to grip it.

594
00:27:40.560 --> 00:27:42.000
None of it's in the episode.

595
00:27:42.420 --> 00:27:44.180
It's in the deleted scenes.

596
00:27:44.180 --> 00:27:49.600
And what was great is over all of this action were two talking heads, one Angela and one

597
00:27:49.600 --> 00:27:50.080
Phyllis.

598
00:27:50.380 --> 00:27:51.260
Can you play those?

599
00:27:51.940 --> 00:27:53.800
I do not mind doing hard labor.

600
00:27:54.380 --> 00:27:58.880
Ronald Reagan got his start as a stock boy lugging heavy boxes 10 hours a day.

601
00:27:59.040 --> 00:27:59.940
Don't miss the pillows.

602
00:28:00.200 --> 00:28:04.440
And he went on to become the president of a party planning committee I like to call the

603
00:28:04.440 --> 00:28:05.580
United States of America.

604
00:28:05.940 --> 00:28:07.100
Most people call it that.

605
00:28:14.110 --> 00:28:18.430
Did you know that an ant can carry five times its own weight?

606
00:28:19.370 --> 00:28:22.250
All it needs is a strong queen to tell it what to do.

607
00:28:22.390 --> 00:28:25.730
And there's nothing that little creature can't accomplish.

608
00:28:27.530 --> 00:28:28.090
Phyllis!

609
00:28:28.130 --> 00:28:29.170
I know!

610
00:28:30.770 --> 00:28:34.330
Phyllis and her power glasses and some serious sass!

611
00:28:34.770 --> 00:28:35.190
Ugh.

612
00:28:35.550 --> 00:28:39.830
Yes, that muffled sound in between was me like falling down the staircase with the Christmas

613
00:28:39.830 --> 00:28:40.170
tree.

614
00:28:40.530 --> 00:28:44.210
Were you so bummed when you watched the episode and it was cut out?

615
00:28:44.230 --> 00:28:47.310
I was so bummed because I thought it was hilarious.

616
00:28:47.310 --> 00:28:52.150
And that talking head I do about Ronald Reagan, my hair is all messed up.

617
00:28:53.110 --> 00:28:53.850
All right.

618
00:28:53.970 --> 00:29:00.250
So Phil Shea has tackled a styrofoam, desk, chair, all objects wrapped in Christmas wrapping.

619
00:29:00.510 --> 00:29:03.130
He's also found Phyllis a pair of power glasses.

620
00:29:03.530 --> 00:29:07.350
Phil Shea's next project would have been Princess Unicorn.

621
00:29:08.250 --> 00:29:08.470
Yes.

622
00:29:08.470 --> 00:29:16.390
Dwight enters with a stack of boxes, and he explains that each year he researches the

623
00:29:16.390 --> 00:29:22.270
most popular toy of the holiday season, he buys as much of it as he can, and then as

624
00:29:22.270 --> 00:29:25.610
parents become more desperate, he sells them at a profit.

625
00:29:25.930 --> 00:29:27.270
It's a little bit genius.

626
00:29:27.770 --> 00:29:32.770
We got a lot of mail asking about this Princess Unicorn storyline.

627
00:29:32.950 --> 00:29:33.290
Okay.

628
00:29:33.290 --> 00:29:34.410
Where to begin?

629
00:29:34.830 --> 00:29:37.750
First of all, this was a collaboration of several writers.

630
00:29:38.490 --> 00:29:44.190
Justin said that they had originally written a different story for Dwight, and at the last

631
00:29:44.190 --> 00:29:45.630
minute, they wanted to change it.

632
00:29:45.970 --> 00:29:52.250
And they had a new writer who had just started on the show that week named Halstead Sullivan.

633
00:29:52.630 --> 00:29:54.550
This was his pitch.

634
00:29:54.890 --> 00:29:55.490
Halstead.

635
00:29:55.730 --> 00:29:56.330
Amazing.

636
00:29:56.630 --> 00:29:59.230
Crushing it in his first week on the job.

637
00:29:59.230 --> 00:30:01.610
We were able to get in touch with Halstead.

638
00:30:01.790 --> 00:30:07.730
He confirmed, yes, that he pitched this idea of Dwight having a side hustle of buying up

639
00:30:07.730 --> 00:30:10.790
these holiday toys and selling them at a profit.

640
00:30:11.750 --> 00:30:16.550
Halstead said that he and writer Aaron Schur were sent into a room to figure out what this

641
00:30:16.550 --> 00:30:17.430
toy should be.

642
00:30:17.990 --> 00:30:21.710
Aaron said, well, kids love princesses and unicorns.

643
00:30:21.810 --> 00:30:23.350
How about a Princess Unicorn doll?

644
00:30:23.550 --> 00:30:25.050
I love this kind of collaboration.

645
00:30:25.050 --> 00:30:29.510
So you have Halstead saying, we need the story of the toy, and he sells the toys.

646
00:30:29.730 --> 00:30:34.130
And then Aaron is like, what about if a unicorn and a doll collide?

647
00:30:34.450 --> 00:30:34.850
Yes.

648
00:30:35.210 --> 00:30:39.230
Then Halstead came up with the catchphrase, my horn can pierce the sky.

649
00:30:39.830 --> 00:30:41.470
Halstead, are you kidding me?

650
00:30:41.550 --> 00:30:41.830
Right?

651
00:30:41.990 --> 00:30:42.750
That was you?

652
00:30:43.010 --> 00:30:45.470
That stuck in our heads forever.

653
00:30:46.150 --> 00:30:46.630
Forever.

654
00:30:47.130 --> 00:30:48.290
Do you remember that, Jenna?

655
00:30:48.410 --> 00:30:48.590
Oh, yeah.

656
00:30:48.590 --> 00:30:49.970
Like, we sang it all week.

657
00:30:49.970 --> 00:30:51.710
We have to hear Michael sing it.

658
00:30:52.470 --> 00:30:55.290
My horn can pierce the sky.

659
00:30:55.730 --> 00:31:00.550
And then Jenna, when I listened to the DVD commentary, immediately Kate and I sang it.

660
00:31:00.810 --> 00:31:01.010
What?

661
00:31:01.710 --> 00:31:04.630
My horn can pierce the sky.

662
00:31:05.470 --> 00:31:06.870
Thank you, Halstead.

663
00:31:07.250 --> 00:31:10.170
Well, you know, they made a whole commercial for this doll.

664
00:31:10.350 --> 00:31:10.910
I know!

665
00:31:11.250 --> 00:31:14.050
With a little girl and a jingle at the end.

666
00:31:14.350 --> 00:31:15.470
It was crazy.

667
00:31:15.750 --> 00:31:17.070
What else did they say about it?

668
00:31:17.070 --> 00:31:23.910
They said, actually, before settling on this idea, there was an alternate idea called Hank Grenade.

669
00:31:24.170 --> 00:31:24.650
Oh.

670
00:31:24.810 --> 00:31:28.930
And this was a doll that when you threw it, his arms blew off.

671
00:31:29.910 --> 00:31:30.330
Oh, my God.

672
00:31:30.330 --> 00:31:31.490
That was Hank Grenade.

673
00:31:31.710 --> 00:31:33.930
But they settled on Princess Unicorn.

674
00:31:35.430 --> 00:31:40.910
So once that was settled, there was a lot of discussion over what she should look like.

675
00:31:41.030 --> 00:31:44.370
Was she a human princess with unicorn features?

676
00:31:44.370 --> 00:31:47.130
Was she more of a horse with a human face?

677
00:31:47.510 --> 00:31:49.530
I guess they went around and around.

678
00:31:50.150 --> 00:31:55.230
And in the end, Phil Shea had to make this Princess Unicorn doll.

679
00:31:55.690 --> 00:32:00.930
Randy told me that Phil actually used a team of designers and toy makers.

680
00:32:01.250 --> 00:32:02.170
Oh, my gosh.

681
00:32:02.170 --> 00:32:06.710
And they had to come up with a design that would not infringe on anyone else's design.

682
00:32:06.710 --> 00:32:13.810
Because I guess toys in general and dolls specifically are very tightly controlled by the manufacturers.

683
00:32:14.150 --> 00:32:14.450
Right.

684
00:32:14.450 --> 00:32:15.970
For their intellectual property rights.

685
00:32:16.210 --> 00:32:16.330
Yeah.

686
00:32:16.430 --> 00:32:18.290
It can't look like anything else.

687
00:32:18.470 --> 00:32:18.850
Yes.

688
00:32:19.150 --> 00:32:29.370
And they actually had to go through the NBC Universal legal team to make sure that they had met all the requirements of a specifically unique doll toy.

689
00:32:29.570 --> 00:32:33.210
That is how we came to have a Princess Unicorn.

690
00:32:33.850 --> 00:32:34.530
Amazing.

691
00:32:34.930 --> 00:32:35.210
Yeah.

692
00:32:36.170 --> 00:32:36.570
Wow.

693
00:32:37.050 --> 00:32:38.970
Phil Shea was so busy this episode.

694
00:32:39.030 --> 00:32:39.450
So busy.

695
00:32:39.650 --> 00:32:40.290
Oh, my gosh.

696
00:32:40.390 --> 00:32:42.010
When we would see him running through the parking lot.

697
00:32:42.210 --> 00:32:42.770
This is why.

698
00:32:43.190 --> 00:32:44.510
I don't know how he did it.

699
00:32:44.610 --> 00:32:44.990
I know.

