00:55:43.270 --> 00:55:44.510
Try to be more interesting.

1274
00:55:45.010 --> 00:55:45.770
Oh, my God.

1275
00:55:45.930 --> 00:55:47.530
And she's like, who else is bored here?

1276
00:55:47.630 --> 00:55:49.550
And like everyone raises their hand.

1277
00:55:49.670 --> 00:55:51.850
She like hijacks the meeting from Michael, right?

1278
00:55:52.110 --> 00:55:54.870
And then she's like, we all do things to cope.

1279
00:55:54.870 --> 00:55:56.190
So I drink when I'm bored.

1280
00:55:56.310 --> 00:55:57.790
And then she goes around the room.

1281
00:55:57.790 --> 00:55:59.870
She goes, you all have coping mechanisMs.

1282
00:55:59.910 --> 00:56:00.610
You eat.

1283
00:56:00.690 --> 00:56:01.150
You eat.

1284
00:56:01.270 --> 00:56:01.730
You eat.

1285
00:56:01.970 --> 00:56:02.790
You shop.

1286
00:56:02.990 --> 00:56:04.530
You confuse Dwight.

1287
00:56:05.190 --> 00:56:06.170
And then she's like.

1288
00:56:06.310 --> 00:56:07.030
Who confuses Dwight, Jim?

1289
00:56:07.130 --> 00:56:07.530
Me.

1290
00:56:07.710 --> 00:56:08.070
No, me.

1291
00:56:08.190 --> 00:56:08.710
Oh, OK.

1292
00:56:09.030 --> 00:56:11.730
And then she like points at Stanley, and she's like, you eat.

1293
00:56:11.810 --> 00:56:16.670
And then Stanley has a talking head where he's like, I do eat when I'm bored, but I also drink.

1294
00:56:16.970 --> 00:56:19.310
And I drink a lot more than Meredith.

1295
00:56:19.530 --> 00:56:21.750
I just don't do it at work, and I keep my clothes on.

1296
00:56:23.150 --> 00:56:24.510
Oh, my goodness.

1297
00:56:24.750 --> 00:56:25.050
Yes.

1298
00:56:25.050 --> 00:56:26.750
This scene was way bigger.

1299
00:56:27.250 --> 00:56:29.110
Oh, wow.

1300
00:56:29.930 --> 00:56:34.630
Michael is going to take Meredith into his office, where they're going to talk for 45 minutes.

1301
00:56:35.130 --> 00:56:36.130
45 minutes.

1302
00:56:36.850 --> 00:56:41.750
And in the meantime, Angela is going to plead with Phyllis.

1303
00:56:41.890 --> 00:56:44.110
Please, can I stop cutting the PETA?

1304
00:56:44.370 --> 00:56:46.430
Do I really have to wear the hairnet?

1305
00:56:46.770 --> 00:56:47.910
Have mercy.

1306
00:56:47.910 --> 00:56:49.530
It's the season of mercy.

1307
00:56:50.050 --> 00:56:51.390
Phyllis is, no.

1308
00:56:51.650 --> 00:56:51.970
Mm-mm.

1309
00:56:52.350 --> 00:56:52.730
No.

1310
00:56:52.970 --> 00:56:54.730
I have a thing I want to point out.

1311
00:56:55.050 --> 00:57:00.750
At 13 minutes, 35 seconds, Phyllis is telling Stanley about the Moroccan food they're eating.

1312
00:57:00.890 --> 00:57:01.170
Mm-hmm.

1313
00:57:01.330 --> 00:57:02.550
And Angela's eating this cookie.

1314
00:57:02.790 --> 00:57:04.030
She spits it out.

1315
00:57:04.350 --> 00:57:04.550
Yeah.

1316
00:57:04.810 --> 00:57:06.350
We did a lot of takes of this.

1317
00:57:06.470 --> 00:57:07.450
I'm not sure why.

1318
00:57:07.750 --> 00:57:07.950
OK.

1319
00:57:07.950 --> 00:57:12.310
But the cookie started to turn on me, because I took a big bite.

1320
00:57:12.430 --> 00:57:12.750
OK.

1321
00:57:13.430 --> 00:57:13.890
Mistake.

1322
00:57:14.210 --> 00:57:14.430
OK.

1323
00:57:14.590 --> 00:57:15.670
Take a small bite, guys.

1324
00:57:15.870 --> 00:57:16.150
Always.

1325
00:57:16.450 --> 00:57:16.750
Always.

1326
00:57:17.110 --> 00:57:21.370
Because by the eighth take, the thought of that cookie makes you want to barf.

1327
00:57:21.530 --> 00:57:21.750
Right.

1328
00:57:22.150 --> 00:57:22.610
And...

1329
00:57:22.610 --> 00:57:23.750
It doesn't matter what it is.

1330
00:57:23.770 --> 00:57:25.930
It doesn't matter if it's your favorite dessert.

1331
00:57:26.330 --> 00:57:26.570
Mm-mm.

1332
00:57:27.090 --> 00:57:28.850
And it started to turn on me.

1333
00:57:28.930 --> 00:57:33.490
And so I took some peanuts, and I stuck them in my hand.

1334
00:57:34.130 --> 00:57:38.430
And when they would cut to me eating, I would, like, just put a bunch of the peanuts in my

1335
00:57:38.430 --> 00:57:39.450
mouth and hold the cookie.

1336
00:57:39.790 --> 00:57:40.130
Oh.

1337
00:57:40.130 --> 00:57:41.550
I was trying to do a fakie eat.

1338
00:57:41.850 --> 00:57:42.250
Mm.

1339
00:57:42.370 --> 00:57:42.930
Fakie eat.

1340
00:57:43.010 --> 00:57:43.430
Fakie eat.

1341
00:57:43.510 --> 00:57:45.710
And then I would spit out peanuts instead of the cookie.

1342
00:57:45.970 --> 00:57:46.250
OK.

1343
00:57:46.790 --> 00:57:49.610
So what we see on camera, that is chewed up peanuts?

1344
00:57:50.010 --> 00:57:50.810
We don't know.

1345
00:57:50.970 --> 00:57:52.050
We don't know which take they used.

1346
00:57:52.050 --> 00:57:53.070
We don't know which take they used.

1347
00:57:53.070 --> 00:57:53.710
Was it early?

1348
00:57:53.790 --> 00:57:54.330
Was it late?

1349
00:57:54.430 --> 00:57:54.990
I don't know.

1350
00:57:55.190 --> 00:57:57.690
These are the things you try to do at work.

1351
00:57:57.750 --> 00:57:59.430
How do I not eat that cookie?

1352
00:57:59.710 --> 00:58:03.810
Well, when Michael leaves his office with Meredith, they're going somewhere.

1353
00:58:04.150 --> 00:58:04.450
Mm-hmm.

1354
00:58:04.450 --> 00:58:06.190
He says, I'll meet you in the parking lot.

1355
00:58:06.190 --> 00:58:10.590
And then he asks Toby for the number of that rehabilitation center.

1356
00:58:10.870 --> 00:58:14.210
And everyone's like, wow, he did it.

1357
00:58:14.450 --> 00:58:14.810
Mm-hmm.

1358
00:58:14.810 --> 00:58:21.190
And then, you know, he finishes writing the number down and he throws the pen at Toby's

1359
00:58:21.190 --> 00:58:21.630
head.

1360
00:58:21.770 --> 00:58:22.990
And hits him in the forehead.

1361
00:58:23.310 --> 00:58:25.450
We got a fan question about that.

1362
00:58:25.670 --> 00:58:27.390
Well, we have stories about it, too.

1363
00:58:29.110 --> 00:58:34.170
Kelsey B would like to know, was the pen throwing scripted or improvised?

1364
00:58:35.050 --> 00:58:36.390
It was scripted.

1365
00:58:36.790 --> 00:58:41.370
And Justin said that Steve had a special rubber pen.

1366
00:58:41.370 --> 00:58:47.410
And I remember it because it was in the pen cup on Pam's desk.

1367
00:58:47.630 --> 00:58:50.910
There were real pens and then one fakie pen.

1368
00:58:51.090 --> 00:58:51.430
Yeah.

1369
00:58:51.490 --> 00:58:58.410
And I was sitting there and I kept, like, positioning the pen so that Steve could pick up the fakie

1370
00:58:58.410 --> 00:58:58.750
pen.

1371
00:58:58.750 --> 00:59:02.910
This would have been another thing Phil Shea would have had to have gotten for the episode.

1372
00:59:03.490 --> 00:59:07.470
Fakie rubber pen so that he could throw it at Toby's head.

1373
00:59:07.470 --> 00:59:09.790
They inserted that little thump sound later.

1374
00:59:10.150 --> 00:59:12.450
We did about four or five takes of it, I guess.

1375
00:59:13.150 --> 00:59:17.570
You guys, if you rewatch this, you will notice behind Michael, there are no people.

1376
00:59:17.750 --> 00:59:20.570
We're all standing way off to the right.

1377
00:59:20.850 --> 00:59:21.050
Yep.

1378
00:59:21.370 --> 00:59:22.090
You want to know why?

1379
00:59:22.290 --> 00:59:23.610
Because we couldn't stop laughing.

1380
00:59:23.950 --> 00:59:28.870
So when they would cut to Michael after throwing it, we'd be behind him giggling.

1381
00:59:29.210 --> 00:59:29.350
Yep.

1382
00:59:29.350 --> 00:59:33.770
So they pushed us all to the right and they had to get our reaction take, like, a whole

1383
00:59:33.770 --> 00:59:36.070
beat later when we had gotten our composure.

1384
00:59:36.410 --> 00:59:38.350
Paul also couldn't stop laughing.

1385
00:59:38.530 --> 00:59:39.110
I know.

1386
00:59:39.290 --> 00:59:42.930
Every time that little rubber pen thumped him in the forehead, he would break.

1387
00:59:43.210 --> 00:59:43.770
I know.

1388
00:59:43.770 --> 00:59:50.590
And there is such a fun blooper where Paul decided to prank Steve during this scene.

1389
00:59:50.590 --> 00:59:51.890
We have to listen to it.

1390
00:59:53.230 --> 00:59:57.350
You know, could you write down the name of that rehabilitation clinic you mentioned?

1391
00:59:57.870 --> 00:59:58.190
Wow.

1392
00:59:58.690 --> 00:59:58.890
Yeah.

1393
01:00:04.140 --> 01:00:04.620
Impressive.

1394
01:00:04.940 --> 01:00:05.380
That's great.

1395
01:00:07.000 --> 01:00:08.140
What does that even say?

1396
01:00:17.960 --> 01:00:22.500
Instead of writing down a fake phone number, he wrote,

1397
01:00:22.720 --> 01:00:23.300
F*** you.

1398
01:00:24.740 --> 01:00:29.000
So Steve in the scene glances down and it says,

1399
01:00:29.240 --> 01:00:29.680
F*** you.

1400
01:00:29.820 --> 01:00:33.140
And he started laughing and he couldn't even throw the pen because he was laughing.

1401
01:00:33.160 --> 01:00:33.680
He was laughing too hard.

1402
01:00:33.780 --> 01:00:35.020
That is so funny.

1403
01:00:35.680 --> 01:00:42.900
Well, I'll have you know, Fakie Pen lived in the pen cup for weeks after we shot the scene

1404
01:00:42.900 --> 01:00:48.480
and people were always coming over trying to grab a pen to use and they would get Fakie

1405
01:00:48.480 --> 01:00:49.160
rubber pen.

1406
01:00:49.740 --> 01:00:53.520
And I never got rid of it because it just was funny to me.

1407
01:00:53.660 --> 01:00:54.020
Yeah.

1408
01:00:54.260 --> 01:00:56.260
It's funny to me that people would grab Fakie Pen.

1409
01:00:56.260 --> 01:00:58.780
So now Meredith and Michael are in the car.

1410
01:00:59.380 --> 01:01:04.180
This is going to start such a fantastic sequence between Meredith and Michael.

1411
01:01:04.600 --> 01:01:07.100
Both Steve and Kate just knock it out of the park.

1412
01:01:07.280 --> 01:01:08.160
They're driving.

1413
01:01:08.340 --> 01:01:09.860
Meredith thinks they're going to a bar.

1414
01:01:10.200 --> 01:01:12.060
She's listing off all these bars.

1415
01:01:12.060 --> 01:01:17.160
And Kate Flannery said in real life, she kept trying to slip her family's bar in there.

1416
01:01:17.400 --> 01:01:21.340
Because you know, her family owned a bar in Philadelphia called Flannery's.

1417
01:01:21.420 --> 01:01:21.600
Yep.

1418
01:01:21.880 --> 01:01:23.200
But it didn't make it in.

1419
01:01:23.460 --> 01:01:27.080
But all the other bars she says are local Scranton bars.

1420
01:01:27.220 --> 01:01:27.860
They're real places.

1421
01:01:28.000 --> 01:01:28.120
Yeah.

1422
01:01:28.180 --> 01:01:31.420
Well, that was part of the reasons why Flannery's wouldn't have checked out, right?

1423
01:01:31.740 --> 01:01:34.980
But she also wanted you guys to know that Steve did his own driving.

1424
01:01:35.280 --> 01:01:36.200
They're not being pulled.

1425
01:01:36.620 --> 01:01:37.000
Yeah.

1426
01:01:37.000 --> 01:01:37.900
You can kind of tell.

1427
01:01:37.900 --> 01:01:41.620
Yeah, he's driving and doing all the dialogue because there were those little lipstick cameras.

1428
01:01:41.900 --> 01:01:48.760
And then they had, I think, a truck in front of them with a camera rigged on the back to get them through the windshield.

1429
01:01:49.300 --> 01:01:55.140
Well, when they finally arrive at their destination, it is revealed that they are at Sunrise Rehab.

1430
01:01:55.500 --> 01:01:57.060
Meredith gets super pissed.

1431
01:01:57.500 --> 01:01:58.620
So pissed.

1432
01:01:59.040 --> 01:02:00.020
So pissed.

1433
01:02:00.180 --> 01:02:04.460
Now, Kate told me they had stunt people there for her and Steve.

1434
01:02:04.900 --> 01:02:08.920
Should it get too physical that they could have this choreographed thing with the stunt people?

1435
01:02:09.120 --> 01:02:10.700
And her and Steve were like, no.

1436
01:02:10.860 --> 01:02:12.020
We're going to go for it.

1437
01:02:12.160 --> 01:02:13.900
Kate was like, Steve, let's do it.

1438
01:02:14.040 --> 01:02:15.880
And they did not use the stunt people.

1439
01:02:16.140 --> 01:02:20.200
Everything you see is actually Kate and Steve just freaking going for it.

1440
01:02:20.320 --> 01:02:22.440
I think I noticed one moment.

1441
01:02:22.440 --> 01:02:24.280
We cut out of it really quickly.

1442
01:02:24.520 --> 01:02:28.700
When Meredith throws the trash can down and it looks like Michael trips and falls,

1443
01:02:28.720 --> 01:02:33.160
I feel like I see Kate start to check on Steve.

1444
01:02:33.660 --> 01:02:34.160
Oh, yeah?

1445
01:02:34.400 --> 01:02:36.120
Like, maybe like, oh, are you okay?

1446
01:02:36.300 --> 01:02:37.820
Like, just the littlest moment.

1447
01:02:37.940 --> 01:02:38.800
And we cut out of it.

1448
01:02:38.920 --> 01:02:42.300
And then they, you know, they have a bigger chase around the parking lot.

1449
01:02:42.540 --> 01:02:44.240
Well, Kate said that's fakie trash.

1450
01:02:44.840 --> 01:02:45.520
Fakie trash?

1451
01:02:45.540 --> 01:02:46.540
That was fakie trash.

1452
01:02:46.540 --> 01:02:48.840
So whatever Steve fell on wasn't real trash.

1453
01:02:49.140 --> 01:02:51.260
So Phil Shea also had to make fakie trash.

1454
01:02:51.540 --> 01:02:51.980
Yes.

1455
01:02:52.140 --> 01:02:52.800
Oh, my gosh.

1456
01:02:52.840 --> 01:02:54.240
This man's week was insane.

1457
01:02:54.540 --> 01:02:54.980
Yes.

1458
01:02:55.120 --> 01:02:58.940
This scene was scripted at the top where she doesn't want to get out of the car.

1459
01:02:58.940 --> 01:03:03.860
But they immediately then just went off, you know, because Paul Feig just wanted them to

1460
01:03:03.860 --> 01:03:06.420
really go for it, not worry about the lines.

1461
01:03:06.900 --> 01:03:12.720
And that whole sequence where Meredith is saying, wait a minute, wait a minute, wait a minute.

1462
01:03:12.840 --> 01:03:13.200
I love that.

1463
01:03:13.300 --> 01:03:14.100
That's not in the script.

1464
01:03:14.120 --> 01:03:14.740
I loved it.

1465
01:03:14.860 --> 01:03:15.840
It was so real.

1466
01:03:15.980 --> 01:03:17.140
It was so real.

1467
01:03:17.280 --> 01:03:18.920
I thought Kate did such a great job.

1468
01:03:19.140 --> 01:03:24.400
Well, this whole thing ends with Michael dragging Meredith into the rehab center.

1469
01:03:24.400 --> 01:03:31.420
And we should tell you, the intake nurse was played by our very own first assistant director,

1470
01:03:31.740 --> 01:03:32.440
Kelly Cantley.

1471
01:03:32.580 --> 01:03:33.060
Yes.

1472
01:03:33.260 --> 01:03:35.540
She also helps escort them out.

1473
01:03:35.640 --> 01:03:41.240
Yeah, at the end, when Michael discovers that you can't force people to go to rehab.

1474
01:03:41.600 --> 01:03:41.960
Yep.

1475
01:03:42.100 --> 01:03:44.420
And now, awkward car ride back.

1476
01:03:44.640 --> 01:03:44.960
Mm-hmm.

1477
01:03:45.100 --> 01:03:46.700
But you know what Michael's going to do?

1478
01:03:47.000 --> 01:03:48.240
Michael's had a realization.

1479
01:03:48.840 --> 01:03:54.620
He realizes that, you know, in order to get help, a person has to hit their rock bottom.

1480
01:03:54.760 --> 01:03:55.060
Mm-hmm.

1481
01:03:55.180 --> 01:04:00.120
So he's going to make it his mission to help Meredith reach her rock bottom.

1482
01:04:00.280 --> 01:04:01.180
Oh, my gosh.

1483
01:04:01.280 --> 01:04:03.420
And he thinks he can do it because he did it with Jan.

1484
01:04:03.800 --> 01:04:04.860
Oh, my gosh.

1485
01:04:04.880 --> 01:04:06.060
Like an amazing line.

1486
01:04:07.420 --> 01:04:10.080
There's still going to be quite a bit of drama back at the office.

1487
01:04:10.300 --> 01:04:10.960
Oh, yes.

1488
01:04:11.300 --> 01:04:12.780
We start with Toby.

1489
01:04:13.800 --> 01:04:14.900
Oh, Toby, man.

1490
01:04:15.120 --> 01:04:17.940
He thinks he's going to get to be the hero to his little girl.

1491
01:04:18.240 --> 01:04:23.520
He is going to score one of the Princess Unicorn dolls from Dwight for his daughter.

1492
01:04:23.780 --> 01:04:25.420
But Dwight has sold them all out.

1493
01:04:25.600 --> 01:04:25.900
Mm-hmm.

1494
01:04:26.000 --> 01:04:28.460
He just sold his last one to Daryl.

1495
01:04:28.580 --> 01:04:28.980
Yes.

1496
01:04:29.500 --> 01:04:30.260
All right.

1497
01:04:30.560 --> 01:04:34.720
I just unsolicited get this email from Jen Salata.

1498
01:04:34.920 --> 01:04:36.020
About this scene?

1499
01:04:36.140 --> 01:04:37.860
About this scene and this episode.

1500
01:04:38.220 --> 01:04:43.920
I guess the writers like Justin and Halstead and Aaron, they were all texting each other

1501
01:04:43.920 --> 01:04:45.880
about this storyline.

1502
01:04:46.200 --> 01:04:47.640
And somehow Jen got involved.

1503
01:04:47.920 --> 01:04:50.180
This email pops in my inbox yesterday.

1504
01:04:50.500 --> 01:04:54.820
She's like, Jenna, we've all been texting about the Princess Unicorn storyline.

1505
01:04:54.820 --> 01:04:56.380
Because you asked Justin about it?

1506
01:04:56.420 --> 01:04:56.660
Yeah.

1507
01:04:56.920 --> 01:04:57.140
Okay.

1508
01:04:57.360 --> 01:04:59.740
And she was like, I have a story.

1509
01:04:59.740 --> 01:05:01.940
And I asked Paul if I could share it.

1510
01:05:02.200 --> 01:05:02.580
Okay.

1511
01:05:02.580 --> 01:05:04.380
And I was like, oh, I'm so intrigued.

1512
01:05:04.680 --> 01:05:06.140
She made an audio clip.

1513
01:05:06.340 --> 01:05:06.760
Here it is.

1514
01:05:06.800 --> 01:05:07.600
Oh, my gosh.

1515
01:05:08.520 --> 01:05:12.460
There was a moment that happened behind the scenes of Moroccan Christmas where Paul and

1516
01:05:12.460 --> 01:05:13.740
I were working on a script together.

1517
01:05:13.980 --> 01:05:17.320
I'm not sure if it was the fifth season finale or what, but we were kind of under the gun,

1518
01:05:17.400 --> 01:05:18.620
I remember, when we were writing.

1519
01:05:19.180 --> 01:05:22.800
And he had to go down on set and shoot a scene as Toby.

1520
01:05:23.220 --> 01:05:26.020
And then when he came back up, we needed to push forward on the script.

1521
01:05:26.340 --> 01:05:31.500
And I remember that he was sitting on the couch and he was like, oh, I think I just screwed

1522
01:05:31.500 --> 01:05:32.740
up that scene that I shot.

1523
01:05:32.860 --> 01:05:34.760
And I was like, I probably didn't.

1524
01:05:34.880 --> 01:05:35.560
I'm sure you didn't.

1525
01:05:35.660 --> 01:05:36.480
